#! mathcas 2 notebook

#% title
# matrix_minimal_polynomial

#% text
# `matrix_minimal_polynomial(m, x)` gives the monic polynomial in `x` of least degree that vanishes at the square matrix `m`.

#% section
# Details

#% item
# It divides the characteristic polynomial and has the same roots.

#% item
# The polynomial is found from the first linear dependence among the powers of `m`.

#% section
# Examples

#% subsection
# Basic examples

#% cell
matrix_minimal_polynomial([[1, 0], [0, 1]], x)
#% output
#= -1 + x

#% cell
matrix_minimal_polynomial([[1, 1], [0, 1]], x)
#% output
#= 1 - 2*x + x^2

#% cell
matrix_minimal_polynomial([[2, 0, 0], [0, 3, 0], [0, 0, 2]], x)
#% output
#= 6 - 5*x + x^2

#% cell
characteristic_polynomial([[2, 0, 0], [0, 3, 0], [0, 0, 2]], x)
#% output
#= -12 + 16*x - 7*x^2 + x^3

